github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested locally on Linux + NVIDIA, it works as expected. I've also tested llvmpipe (software Vulkan rendering) and it also works correctly there, although grid rendering is broken regardless of the line width used (other gizmos are fine).\r\n\r\nCode looks good to me.\r\n\r\nNote that this PR doesn't implement wide lines in Direct3D 12, Metal or Compatibility yet. It's not feasible to support Metal given API and hardware limitations, but OpenGL should be possible (and possibly Direct3D 12).\r\n\r\nI think in the long run, we'll want an universal way to emulate thick line drawing using screen-aligned quads. This will work on every graphics API and hardware combination, including Metal and WebGL where thick lines are normally not available at all. We already use this for the [3D editor origin](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/83895). This way, we can have optional fast antialiasing on a per-line basis, without needing MSAA or TAA.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106330#pullrequestreview-2837136035","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106330","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106330#pullrequestreview-2837136035"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106330"}},"submitted_at":"2025-05-13T14:57:04Z","commit_id":null}]